label: Bond Ratings
description: Credit rating reference records with public credit-quality context.
catalog: exchange_traded_funds_large
schema: public
table_name: bond_ratings
dimensions:
  credit_quality:
    description: Unique credit rating designation (e.g., 'AAA', 'AA', 'A', 'BBB', 'BB', 'B', 'Below B', 'US Government'). Must be unique across all records.
    label: Credit Quality
    sql: credit_scoringmark
    ai_context: 'Credit Quality: Indicates the creditworthiness of the bonds a fund holds. ''Government'' is the highest quality. ''AAA'' and ''AA'' are considered high-grade investment quality. Ratings below ''BBB'' are considered speculative or high-yield.'
